ing all  of those things labour have called on  the home secretary to introduce but the  homestead she's failed to do so we've  also faced a decade of austerity with  police numbers being uh cut again  something that we have repeatedly called  on the home secretary to look at  should they reexamine the parties in  number 10 and downing street sorry in  downing street and whitehall  look the  that's a matter for  the police but i think that you know the  people have been incredibly shocked with  what they have seen from downing street  whilst the  public were sticking by the rules making  huge sacrifices uh i've had constituents  contact me  about not being  fathers not being there for the birth of  their children  family members not being able to say  goodbye to  loved ones  the public are rightly outraged by the  fact that whilst that was going on there  were parties taking place in downing  street the prime minister has been  we know all of that i'm just wondering  whether you would be calling us part of  the special measures the metropolitan  police has been told it hasn't done its  job on a number of things properly um  would you be calling for that to be  re-examined those parties well i think  we need to look at that really uh  closely in the the next few uh weeks um  to see if mistakes were made we need to  get a new met commissioner in place uh i  want to see a reforming commissioner  in place to clear up the mess in the met  to restore public confidence and make  sure that if mistakes have been made  they are put right but we need to get  that reforming new mech commissioner in  place uh to do that  and finally there seems to be some  ambivalence in your party uh about the  many strikes taking place uh what is  your personal position do you support  them  the issue on the strikes is  really a government failure to get round  the the table we saw the rail strikes  last week the government should have  been in those negotiations with the rail  companies with 